by dylan-rumble at 2026-09-28T09:12:38Z

The Psalm failure is not new. The two `InvalidReturnStatement` errors in `ObjectMapper::map()` (it returns `object` where the interface declares the template `T`) already exist on 7.4, at the same two `return $this->doMap(...)` lines.

The job builds a baseline from 7.4, and Psalm matches baseline entries by the text of the code. This PR adds `$constructTarget` to those two lines, so the old entries no longer match and are reported again. I reproduced this locally with the same baseline steps. I left the code as it is rather than changing it only to satisfy the baseline.
